# Env files are NEVER committed — not even dotenvx-encrypted ones. Ciphertext in
# a repo is only as safe as the private key, and the key outlives the repo.
# `.env.example` is the one exception: it holds names and placeholders only.
.env
.env.*
*.local
.env.keys
!.env.example
